    --------------------------
    The KGCL command line tool
    --------------------------

The KGCL command line tool

  KGCL-Java comes with a standalone tool to manipulate KGCL changesets
  from the command line.

  The <<<kgcl-cli>>> commands act as Unix filter that reads one or more
  KGCL changeset either from files or from standard input (or both), and
  writes the changeset back to standard output.

  It can be used to:

  * catenate several changesets into a single changeset;

  * convert changeset from one format to another;

  * check that a changeset is syntactically correct.

* Basic usage

  The following call:

+----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ kgcl-cli -o all.yaml set1.kgcl set2.yaml set3.json
+----------------------------------------------------------------------

  will read KGCL changesets from the <<<set1.kgcl>>>, <<<set2.yaml>>>,
  and <<<set3.json>>> files, merge them together, and write the result
  in the <<<all.yaml>>> file.

* Input options

  Changesets are read either from files given as positional arguments
  or, without any positional argument, from standard input.

  The special name <<<->>> can also be used to explicitly read from
  standard input.

  When reading from a file, the format of the file is inferred, if
  possible, from the file’s extension. If the extension is not
  recognized, or when reading from standard input, the format is
  assumed to be KGCL.

  Use the <<<--input-format>>> option to force the expected input
  format instead of inferring it from extensions. Of note, that option
  applies to all input files.

* Output options

  By default, the result changeset is written to standard output in KGCL
  format.

  Use the <<<--output>>> option to send the output to a file. The file’s
  extension will be used to infer the output format.

  Use the <<<--output-format>>> to explicitly specify the format.
